    <!-- Help -->
    <string name="help_title">Help &amp; FAQ</string>
    <string name="help_q1">Why can\'t my phone see the other one?</string>
    <string name="help_a1">Both phones must be on the same Wi-Fi network, or within Bluetooth range for Nearby. Some routers isolate clients from each other — the Connection Doctor reports that case. Turning Wi-Fi off and on again re-sends the discovery beacon.</string>
    <string name="help_q2">Does Morsecode use the internet?</string>
    <string name="help_a2">No. Transfers run over your local network or Nearby. There are no accounts, no cloud storage and no analytics; the only network traffic is between the two devices.</string>
    <string name="help_q3">A transfer stopped halfway. Is it lost?</string>
    <string name="help_a3">No. Every confirmed offset is stored, so Retry continues from the last acknowledged byte instead of restarting the file.</string>
    <string name="help_q4">Where do received files go?</string>
    <string name="help_a4">Into the folder you granted under Storage access. Photos, videos and music are also added to the media library so other apps can see them.</string>
    <string name="help_q5">Can a laptop join without the app?</string>
    <string name="help_a5">Yes. Turn on WebShare and open the printed address in any browser on the same network. Each browser session must be approved on the phone and can be revoked at any time.</string>
    <string name="help_q6">Transfers stop when the screen turns off.</string>
    <string name="help_a6">Request a battery optimization exemption in Settings. Android otherwise suspends background work within minutes.</string>
    <string name="help_troubleshoot">Troubleshooting</string>
    <string name="help_open_doctor">Open Connection Doctor</string>

